.TH LOGIC 1
.SH NAME
logic \- truth-table gate synthesizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/logic
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Logic
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Apps/Logic
truth-table gate synthesizer.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Give it the columns of a truth table and it builds a circuit that
produces them, by repeated passes over a table of every value the
circuit can hold, adding whichever gate it can make from values it
already has.
All values are hexadecimal.
.PP
The fields are:
.TP
.B Table size
The number of table entries, and so the width of a column:
.B 100
for three inputs,
.B 10000
for four.
The original's maximum is
.BR 10000 .
.TP
.B Input columns
Any number of input columns, separated by spaces.
The default
.B "F0 CC AA"
is the three-input enumeration.
.TP
.B Output columns
Any number of columns to be produced.
.TP
.B Gates
The gate types the synthesizer may use, in the order it should try
them.
The order matters: each pass tries the gates in the order given, so
listing
.B NAND
before
.B AND
yields a different circuit.
The names are
.BR NOT ,
.BR AND ,
.BR OR ,
.BR NAND ,
.BR NOR ,
.BR XOR ,
.BR AND3 ,
.BR OR3 ,
.BR NAND3 ,
.BR NOR3 .
.PP
.B "Run synthesis"
fills the table, reporting each pass, and then draws the circuit
right to left in the panel below \- gate sprites, red connection
wires, green input letters and
.B Dup
labels, and each node's value in black.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "Run synthesis"
.TP
.B "Run synthesis"
Synthesize and draw the circuit
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /icons/temple/logic_1.bit
Gate sprites, one pair of
.IB name .bit
and
.IB name .mask
per gate type, rasterized from the
.B $SP
bins of the original
.BR Logic.HC .
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/logic.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The original re-dumps the schematic into a scrolling document on every
synthesis; here it persists in the panel.
